VERSION 1
WHEN PRESENT \bsetrlimit\s*\(\s*RLIMIT_CORE\s*,\s*(?:0|NULL|nullptr)\s*\)
REPORT AS area_of_interest
REASON Review a null rlimit pointer passed to setrlimit. This does not configure zero limits; check the return value and pass a correctly initialized struct rlimit when disabling core dumps.
TRACE Externalized rule logic for Improper Use of `setrlimit` for Core Dump Prevention.
